From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Stoffel <stoffel.thomas.ryan@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 04:02:17 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] build: keep the Copilot SDK in the local copilot extension
 build

`gulp vscode-darwin-<arch>-min` compiles the built-in copilot extension
from source and filters its node_modules through build/.moduleignore.
That file drops @github/copilot, which the app's own node_modules do not
need, so the extension loses it too. Packaging then fails in
prepareBuiltInCopilotRipgrepShim, which expects the extension's
node_modules/@github/copilot/sdk.

Upstream's product builds never take this path: they package the
extension from a prebuilt Copilot VSIX. Add back the parts of
@github/copilot that the VSIX ships (extensions/copilot/.vscodeignore):
its package.json and sdk/. The rest, such as its clipboard module with
binaries for both Mac architectures, stays out, as it does in the VSIX.

diff --git a/build/lib/extensions.ts b/build/lib/extensions.ts
index 10bd9fbd693b764a952fb52d7d97c6a07a676f85..a93d1c2ab7902b9b0640bfbd3649005dfba3a114 100644
--- a/build/lib/extensions.ts
+++ b/build/lib/extensions.ts
@@ -483,7 +483,11 @@ export function packageCopilotExtensionStream(): Stream {
 		localExtensionsStream,
 		gulp.src(dependenciesSrc, { base: '.' })
 			.pipe(util2.cleanNodeModules(path.join(root, 'build', '.moduleignore')))
-			.pipe(util2.cleanNodeModules(path.join(root, 'build', `.moduleignore.${process.platform}`)))
+			.pipe(util2.cleanNodeModules(path.join(root, 'build', `.moduleignore.${process.platform}`))),
+		gulp.src([
+			'extensions/copilot/node_modules/@github/copilot/package.json',
+			'extensions/copilot/node_modules/@github/copilot/sdk/**'
+		], { base: '.' })
 	).pipe(util2.setExecutableBit(['**/*.sh']));
 }
 
